          "date": "2026-08-26 12:03:23.000000000",
          "tz": 120
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Marc Vef",
          "email": "mvef@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-08-26 12:34:46.000000000",
          "tz": 120
        },
        "subject": "LU-10026 llite: skip layout changes if update is held",
        "message": "LU-10026 llite: skip layout changes if update is held\n\nskip minor layout changes (like incompressability) when the client\nhelds UPDATE lock as MDT grabs UPDATE lock for this kind of changes.\n\nllite: do not update layout from fsync\n\nfsync can be called from within write. in this case there would be one\nactive IO (from LOV's point of view). if we update the layout at this\npoint, then fsync would need to refresh the layout to proceed, but\ngiven there is an active IO, LOV would block layout refresh waiting\nfor all IOs to finish - a dealock.\n\nDDN-bug-id: EX-10979\nWas-Change-Id: I6d1cd7787f4c0d9f75f01030ed1235279bb6d301\n\nllite: do not update layout at umount\n\numount can race with ptlrpcd finishing IOs and locks.\nat the same time, umount resets sb->s_root to NULL which\nis needed to form new RPCs, so it's safer to skip minor\nlayout update.\n\nDDN-bug-id: EX-11166\nWas-Change-Id: Ie9df33e95317bf38452ddd3afdfa30b31932bdb4\n\nTest-Parameters: forjanitoronly\nDDN-bug-id: EX-10857\nSigned-off-by: Alex Zhuravlev <bzzz@whamcloud.com>\nSigned-off-by: Marc Vef <mvef@whamcloud.com>\nChange-Id: I52e31a9c15967dd92714e6102e6b16d22695f81b\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
